      "choice": "Compare each bar's High/Low against the fixed stop level (intrabar breach), not just the Close",
      "reason": "Spec states a protective stop-loss level but not the exact intrabar detection mechanism; High/Low breach is the standard literal reading of a stop order."
    },
    {
      "topic": "atr_at_entry",
      "choice": "entry_price and the ATR reading used for the stop are taken at the bar where the order actually fills (order.executed.price / self.atr[0] in notify_order), not the bar where the crossover signal fired",
      "reason": "Backtrader's default broker fills market orders at the next bar's open, so 'entry_price' and the ATR value at entry are read at the actual fill to match real position entry."
    },
    {
